q35 for the update test in QEMU (tools/build.sh update-test), never in a
W541 ROM: build.sh applies it to a git worktree of the coreboot tree of its
own, which only builds the ROMs for QEMU.

- vboot's nvdata in the flash (RW_NVRAM), as on the W541. verstage runs in
  the bootblock, which executes from the pflash; while the pflash takes
  commands, QEMU reads back its status there, not code, so the loops that
  write and erase it run from .data, in RAM. romstage and postcar only
  read it; ramstage and SMM write with ../qemu-i440fx/rom_media.c.
- only the bootblock with verstage in the read-only CBFS, the rest in the
  RW slots (RW_REGION_ONLY), like LENOVO_HASWELL_VBOOT_MINIMAL_RO.
- update-test.fmd: the W541's flash map cut down to the regions a capsule
  update reads or writes, in an 8 MiB pflash.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
